# Freyalise's Winds: "Whenever a permanent becomes tapped, put a wind counter on it. If a permanent with a wind counter on it
# would untap during its controller's untap step, remove all wind counters from it instead." (CR 603.2, 614.1a, 502.3)
# Bot1's Mox Emerald is tapped to cast it, before it is on the battlefield: no counter, and it untaps on turn three. Bot1's
# Forest is tapped for mana, untapped by Twiddle - an effect's untap, no untap step's, so the counter stays - and tapped
# again: two wind counters. On turn three it stays tapped and both come off (all of them, not one); Mox Sapphire, tapped
# once, likewise. Bot2's Forest, tapped on turn two, keeps its counter through Bot1's untap step (not its controller's)
# and loses it, staying tapped, in Bot2's on turn four. With no counter left, Bot1's Forest untaps on turn five.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Freyalise's Winds
Mox Sapphire
Twiddle
Island
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest x25

